WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.968
[music playing]

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:05.538
NARRATOR: As experts begin to
search for other explanations,

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.407
they turn their
attention to a series

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:10.043
of disturbing
discoveries that occurred

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:14.414
in the months following
the June 2012 attacks.

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:16.850
We had some dolphins that
washed up already dead.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.087
We weren't really
sure what it was,

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.655
but we did hear
from other states

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:26.226
that they were having
the same issue.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:30.930
NARRATOR: In fact, it turns out
that over the course of 2013,

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:37.370
a total of 48 dolphins are found
dead on South Carolina beaches.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:40.607
Researchers concluded the
dolphins were inflicted

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.041
with the morbillivirus.

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:49.482
This deadly disease suppresses
the dolphin's immune system

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:52.385
and causes inflammation
of the brain.

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:56.122
The result is a bizarre
shift in behavior.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.957
Infected dolphins
have been witnessed

00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:02.862
swimming in strange patterns,
almost like they are drunk.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:05.632
And additional
research has shown

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:08.668
that brain inflammation
in zebrafish

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.904
caused them to
become more agitated.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:18.878
So in 2012, could the
sharks of Myrtle Beach

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:21.247
have been inflicted
with a disease that

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:23.817
changed their
behavior, making them

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.385
more likely to bite swimmers?

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:32.058
According to Dr. Dan
Huber, it comes down

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.427
to a shark's immune system.

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:35.862
DAN HUBER: For
animals, the skin is

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.730
the first line of
defense against any type

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:39.032
of an infection.

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:42.635
So the skin is part of the
immune system, essentially.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.871
Looking at a section of
shark skin which shows what

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:46.639
are called dermal
denticles, which

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:50.643
are basically little teeth that
make up the scales of a shark.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.012
NARRATOR: The denticles
perform a unique function

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:55.615
in the shark's immune system.

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.083
DAN HUBER: Dermal
denticles creates

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.985
a very uneven
shape that bacteria

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.653
have a hard time adhering to.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.388
Because the bacteria
can't adhere to it,

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.756
they can't form colonies.

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.058
And this is something
that helps sharks

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:09.295
to resist bacterial infections.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.831
NARRATOR: And there's also
another organ that helps

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.233
protect sharks from disease--

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:18.271
their liver.

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:23.109
The liver produces a chemical
compound called squalamine.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:27.981
The squalamine is dispersed
inside the shark's cells.

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:31.351
If a virus invades the
cells, the squalamine

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:36.089
prevents it from multiplying
so the virus doesn't spread.

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:39.259
And the shark doesn't get sick.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:43.029
Scientists are even testing
squalamine to fight cancer

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:45.465
in humans.

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:48.201
This remarkable
immune system means

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:50.169
that sharks might
be one of the most

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:53.740
disease-resistant
creatures on Earth.

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:56.209
Any suggestion that the
sharks could have become ill due

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:58.344
to a virus or a
bacterial infection

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.046
isn't very likely
because sharks have

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.881
very strong immune systems.

